{
  "_comment": [
    "What a staff drink is given for free. Written down once and executed on both sides.",
    "Committed VERBATIM to MadarRust tests/fixtures/ and madar/rust-core/crates/madar-core/tests/fixtures/.",
    "Executed by MadarRust tests/staff_comp_vectors_tests.rs against src/staff_pool/comp.rs.",
    "These are the specification. Change the rule HERE first and let both repos fail until they agree.",
    "THE RULE. A staff drink is a normal sale whose pooled line is comped on its BASE CONFIGURATION only.",
    "1. SIZE: the free amount is the price of the CHEAPEST ACTIVE size (branch_price wins over price). A larger size pays the difference. `sizes` empty (no sizes, or the line names none) or no active size: `unit_price` is the free amount. size_comp = min(free_size, unit_price).",
    "2. OPTIONAL add-ons (picks whose option is in no group with required_min >= 1) and `optionals_per_unit`: never free.",
    "3. REQUIRED groups (required_min >= 1): allowance = price of the first ACTIVE option flagged is_default x required_min; with none, the CHEAPEST active option x required_min; no active option: 0. The picks made in the group (unit_price x quantity each, as they RANG) are comped up to the allowance, in pick order; the rest is paid. Never negative: a cheaper pick earns no credit for another group or for the size. A pick belongs to the first required group listing its option.",
    "4. free_per_unit = min(normal_per_unit, size_comp + sum of group comps); charged_per_unit = normal_per_unit - free_per_unit. A line of n units is n times each (line_comp, line_charged).",
    "5. eligible=false (the pool decision refused the line) comps nothing.",
    "All amounts are integer minor units (piastres). No figure is ever rounded. Negative inputs are read as 0.",
    "Prices are the prices AS THEY RING ON THE LINE. A swap group (milk, beans) already rings as a difference over the recipe's own ingredient, so callers never pass it as a required group: its picks are plain extras.",
    "Tax, service and any order-level discount are computed on the CHARGED part only, by the bill engine (tax_vectors.json): the comp is taken off the line before the subtotal is formed."
  ],
